<h1>Policy Quote Comparison</h1>

<p>
    The Policy Quote Comparison tool extracts text from both a bound policy document and a renewal quote, then uses AI to generate a detailed comparison highlighting differences, changes, and important updates between the two documents.
</p>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Screenshot of the Policy Quote Comparison tool showing: policy document selector, quote document selector, comparison progress indicator, and the resulting comparison report with highlighted differences. Show the side-by-side or before/after view of key changes. -->

<h2>What the Policy Quote Comparison Does</h2>

<p>
    This tool helps you:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Compare documents</strong> – Analyze both the expiring policy and the renewal quote side-by-side</li>
    <li><strong>Extract text automatically</strong> – Uses document intelligence to pull text from PDFs</li>
    <li><strong>Identify differences</strong> – Highlights what changed between the old policy and new quote</li>
    <li><strong>Generate AI summary</strong> – Creates a narrative comparison explaining key changes</li>
    <li><strong>Save time</strong> – Automates the tedious process of manually comparing long policy documents</li>
    <li><strong>Cache results</strong> – Saves extracted text for faster re-comparisons</li>
</ul>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Visual diagram showing the comparison workflow: 1) Select policy and quote PDFs, 2) Extract text from both, 3) AI analyzes differences, 4) Generate comparison report, 5) Review changes. Use icons and progress indicators. -->

<h2>Using the Policy Quote Comparison</h2>

<p>
    To compare a policy and quote:
</p>

<ol>
    <li><strong>Open from a renewal</strong> – Launch the tool from a renewal page so it has context about the policy and available quotes</li>
    <li><strong>Select the policy document</strong> – Choose the bound policy PDF you want to compare (usually the expiring policy)</li>
    <li><strong>Select the quote document</strong> – Choose the renewal quote PDF you want to compare against</li>
    <li><strong>Start the comparison</strong> – Click <strong>Compare</strong> to begin the process</li>
    <li><strong>Monitor progress</strong> – Watch the progress indicator as it:
        <ul>
            <li>Extracts text from the quote document</li>
            <li>Extracts text from the policy document</li>
            <li>Generates the AI comparison</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Review the results</strong> – Once complete, review the comparison report showing:
        <ul>
            <li>Document statistics (page count, word count)</li>
            <li>AI-generated comparison narrative</li>
            <li>Key differences and changes</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
</ol>

