<h2>Debug Mode</h2>

<p>
    Debug mode allows you to:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Reuse cached text</strong> – Skip PDF processing and use previously extracted text files</li>
    <li><strong>Faster comparisons</strong> – Run comparisons much faster when you've already extracted text</li>
    <li><strong>Test AI changes</strong> – Re-run the AI comparison with different prompts or settings</li>
    <li><strong>Inspect extracted text</strong> – View the raw extracted text files if needed</li>
</ul>

<p>
    <strong>When to use debug mode:</strong>
</p>
<ul>
    <li>You've already run a comparison and want to try different AI prompts</li>
    <li>You want to save time by skipping PDF extraction</li>
    <li>You need to inspect the extracted text for troubleshooting</li>
</ul>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Screenshot showing the debug mode toggle and the option to "Compare Using Saved Text". Show where cached text files are stored and how to access them. -->

<h2>Running AI Comparison on Cached Text</h2>

<p>
    After extracting text, you can run the AI comparison separately:
</p>

<ol>
    <li>Complete a full comparison first (this extracts and caches the text)</li>
    <li>Use the <strong>Run OpenAI on Cached Text</strong> option</li>
    <li>The AI will analyze the cached text files without re-processing the PDFs</li>
    <li>This is useful if you want to:
        <ul>
            <li>Try different comparison prompts</li>
            <li>Re-run the analysis after updating AI settings</li>
            <li>Get a fresh comparison without waiting for PDF extraction</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
</ol>

