<h2>Best Practices</h2>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Use during renewals</strong> – Compare the expiring policy with renewal quotes to identify changes</li>
    <li><strong>Review carefully</strong> – AI comparisons are helpful but should be reviewed for accuracy</li>
    <li><strong>Check important sections</strong> – Pay special attention to coverage limits, deductibles, and exclusions</li>
    <li><strong>Use cached text for speed</strong> – Once text is extracted, use debug mode for faster re-comparisons</li>
    <li><strong>Share with clients</strong> – Use the comparison report to explain changes to clients</li>
    <li><strong>Document changes</strong> – Save comparison reports as attachments for your records</li>
</ul>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Visual checklist showing best practices with icons: renewal icon, review icon, important sections icon, sharing icon. -->

<h2>What Gets Compared</h2>

<p>
    The AI comparison analyzes:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Coverage limits</strong> – Changes in liability limits, property values, etc.</li>
    <li><strong>Deductibles</strong> – Changes in deductible amounts</li>
    <li><strong>Coverage types</strong> – Additions or removals of specific coverages</li>
    <li><strong>Exclusions</strong> – Changes to policy exclusions</li>
    <li><strong>Terms and conditions</strong> – Updates to policy language</li>
    <li><strong>Premiums</strong> – Changes in premium amounts (if visible in documents)</li>
    <li><strong>Effective dates</strong> – Policy period changes</li>
</ul>

