<h2>Troubleshooting</h2>

<h3>Documents Not Extracting</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Ensure both documents are PDFs (not images or other formats)</li>
    <li>Check that the documents are not password-protected or corrupted</li>
    <li>Verify document intelligence integration is configured (Azure or LLMWhisperer)</li>
    <li>Try processing the documents individually first to identify which one has issues</li>
</ul>

<h3>AI Comparison Not Generating</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Verify OpenAI integration is configured and working</li>
    <li>Check that text extraction completed successfully for both documents</li>
    <li>Ensure documents are not too large (very long documents may be truncated)</li>
    <li>Try running the AI comparison on cached text if the initial attempt failed</li>
</ul>

<h3>Comparison Results Seem Incomplete</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Very long documents may be truncated to fit AI model limits</li>
    <li>Check the document statistics to see if truncation occurred</li>
    <li>Review the cached text files to see what was actually extracted</li>
    <li>Consider comparing specific sections if documents are very long</li>
</ul>

<h3>Debug Mode Not Working</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Ensure you've run a full comparison first to create cached text files</li>
    <li>Check that cached text files exist and are accessible</li>
    <li>Verify the file paths shown in the comparison results</li>
</ul>

